Title: The Orchard House
Credit: Table Read entity-inference fixture (T7.17)
Author: Fixture
Draft date: 2026-07-16

# Planted (never stated literally): Dorothy/Dot and Marguerite/Margo are each
# one person under two names; Owen never gets a dialogue cue; Dorothy and
# Marguerite share a grandmother and a family relationship that is implied,
# never named directly; Owen's wariness toward both of them is implied, never
# named. Two locations (greenhouse, boathouse) and one recurring object (the
# brass key) carry across both scenes.

INT. GREENHOUSE - DAY

DOROTHY ASHWORTH-KANE stands over a row of orchids, still wearing her mother's gardening gloves.

MARGUERITE
Dot, you're not supposed to be in here.

DOROTHY ASHWORTH-KANE
(not looking up)
Margo, it's my greenhouse too.

In the corner, OWEN polishes a brass key without a word, careful not to look at either of them.

MARGUERITE
(lower, so Owen won't hear)
Grandmother left this place to both of us, remember? Not just you.

She nods toward the key still turning in Owen's fingers.

EXT. BOATHOUSE - DUSK

Dorothy walks the dock alone, the same brass key glinting now in her own palm. Owen watches from the greenhouse window, arms crossed, and does not follow.
